# What must never enter a build context.
#
# THIS FILE PREVIOUSLY CONTAINED ONE LINE: "data". Everything else in the working
# directory was copied into the image by `COPY . .`, and two of those things are
# credentials.
#
# .env is the deployment's own secrets — database password, the KEKs that decrypt
# everything at rest, third-party API keys. It is gitignored, so it never reached
# the repository, but `docker build .` runs in the DEPLOYMENT directory where the
# real one lives, and it was being baked into the image. Anyone able to pull or
# inspect that image had the workspace's keys.
#
# firebase-cred.json is a service-account private key.
#
# Neither is needed to compile anything.
.env
.env.*
*.env
firebase-cred.json
*-cred.json
*.pem
*.key

# Not needed by the build, and large.
.git
.github
data
node_modules
*.tar.gz
*.dump
*.log
